        <div class="hotels-stop-head">
          <h3>Kyoto <span style="font-weight:400;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-soft);">· 40K cert candidate</span></h3>
          <span class="stop-meta">Tue Jul 21 → Sat Jul 25 · 4 nights · Westin Miyako = Bonvoy Cat 5</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hotels-grid"><div class="veg-loading">Loading hotel rates…</div></div>
      </div>

    </div>
     </div>
     <aside class="section-map-split__map" data-trip-map="hotels" aria-label="Map of hotels"></aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== TRANSPORT ========== -->
<section class="transport" id="transport">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="section-eyebrow">Ground transport</div>
        <h2>Every drive, ride, and rail <em>booked in advance</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>Japan rewards pre-booking: Shinkansen seats sell out for early-morning trains, Hakone day-pass saves ~40% vs single tickets, and Narita arrival-day taxi is more sane than Keisei Skyliner with two tired kids and 4 suitcases.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="transport-grid">

      <div class="car-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="car-head">
          <div class="car-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-car"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h4>Home → BLR T2 (outbound)</h4>
            <div class="car-leg">Fri Jul 10 · Evening airport run</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="car-detail">For an international 06:00 departure, leave home by 02:30. Pre-book Uber Reserve 48h prior — early-morning surge is real. Family of 4 + 4 large suitcases needs Uber XL or Ola Prime SUV. Reach BLR T2 by 03:30 for a 4h check-in window.</p>
        <div class="car-stats">
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Distance</div><div class="car-stat-val">~40 km</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Drive</div><div class="car-stat-val">~1 hr (off-peak)</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Est.</div><div class="car-stat-val">₹1.8–2.5K</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="car-providers">
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://m.uber.com/reserve/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Uber Reserve</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://book.olacabs.com/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Ola Prime</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.savaari.com/airport-transfer/bengaluru-airport-cabs/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Savaari</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="car-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="car-head">
          <div class="car-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-car"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h4>Narita Airport → JW Marriott Tokyo</h4>
            <div class="car-leg">Sat Jul 11 · Arrival transfer</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="car-detail">Pre-book a private van via Klook or Welcome Pickups. After 14h+ in transit with two kids, a fixed-price van with a name-board pickup is worth the ₹2K premium over Skyliner+taxi. Skyliner+local cab is the budget option (~₹6K total) but punishing with luggage.</p>
        <div class="car-stats">
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Distance</div><div class="car-stat-val">~75 km</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Drive</div><div class="car-stat-val">~75 min</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Est.</div><div class="car-stat-val">¥18-25K (₹10-14K)</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="car-providers">
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.klook.com/en-IN/activity/2107-narita-airport-private-transfer-tokyo/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Klook private van</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.welcomepickups.com/tokyo/airport-taxi/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Welcome Pickups</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.keisei.co.jp/keisei/tetudou/skyliner/us/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Keisei Skyliner</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="car-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="car-head">
          <div class="car-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-train"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h4>Tokyo → Kyoto (Shinkansen Nozomi)</h4>
            <div class="car-leg">Tue Jul 21 · Bullet train </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="car-detail">Nozomi is the fastest (2h 15m, Tokyo Station → Kyoto Station). Reserved seats only — book on Smart-EX (JR Central app, English, foreign cards accepted). Pick the right side coming from Tokyo for Mt. Fuji view (~40 min in). 1 large suitcase per person fits overhead; oversized luggage requires advance reservation.</p>
        <div class="car-stats">
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Distance</div><div class="car-stat-val">~520 km</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Time</div><div class="car-stat-val">2h 15m</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Est.</div><div class="car-stat-val">¥14K × 4 (₹32K)</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="car-providers">
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://smart-ex.jp/en/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Smart-EX (JR app)</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.klook.com/en-IN/activity/27840-shinkansen-bullet-train-japan/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Klook Shinkansen</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Tokyo+Station/Kyoto+Station" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-route"/></svg> Route</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="car-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="car-head">
          <div class="car-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-train"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h4>Day trips from Tokyo — Fuji · Hakone · Kamakura</h4>
            <div class="car-leg">Jul 17 / 19 / 18 · same-day return to JW</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="car-detail">All three nature trips run as day trips from the JW base, so bags never move. <strong>Kawaguchiko/Fuji</strong> (Jul 17): highway bus from Shinjuku (~2h, reserve ahead) or JR via Otsuki. <strong>Hakone loop</strong> (Jul 19): Odakyu Romance Car Shinjuku → Hakone-Yumoto (85 min), then the Hakone Free Pass covers the whole loop. <strong>Kamakura</strong> (Jul 18): JR Yokosuka line from Tokyo Station (~1h), Enoden line on arrival. Buy the Romance Car + Free Pass online; use Suica for Kamakura.</p>
        <div class="car-stats">
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Fuji</div><div class="car-stat-val">~2.5h each way</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Hakone</div><div class="car-stat-val">85 min + Free Pass</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Kamakura</div><div class="car-stat-val">~1h each way</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="car-providers">
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.odakyu.jp/english/romancecar/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Romance Car (Hakone)</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.odakyu.jp/english/passes/hakone/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Hakone Free Pass</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.highwaybus.com/gp/index" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Fuji highway bus</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="car-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="car-head">
          <div class="car-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-train"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h4>Kyoto → Kansai Airport (KIX)</h4>
            <div class="car-leg">Sat Jul 25 · Haruka Express </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="car-detail">JR Haruka limited express runs Kyoto Station → KIX in ~75 min, all-reserved. The trip ends in Kyoto (open-jaw return from KIX), so there's no Shinkansen backtrack to Tokyo — saves the better part of a travel day. Buy the ICOCA &amp; Haruka discount package or reserve on Smart-EX. Light bags only by this point.</p>
        <div class="car-stats">
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Time</div><div class="car-stat-val">~75 min</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Est.</div><div class="car-stat-val">¥3.6K × 4</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Reserve</div><div class="car-stat-val">all-reserved</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="car-providers">
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.westjr.co.jp/global/en/ticket/pass/haruka/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Haruka Express</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Kyoto+Station/Kansai+International+Airport" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-route"/></svg> Route</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="car-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="car-head">
          <div class="car-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-route"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h4>Daily intra-city — Tokyo + Kyoto</h4>
            <div class="car-leg">Jul 11 → Jul 24 · Suica IC + walking</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="car-detail">Get a Suica IC card on arrival (mobile via Apple Wallet preferred — works for trains, buses, vending machines, conbini). For evening with tired kids, taxis are clean + metered + safe (~₹500-1500 per ride in central Tokyo). Uber is sparse outside central Tokyo — use the standard taxi flag-down or the GO taxi app.</p>
        <div class="car-stats">
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Suica top-up</div><div class="car-stat-val">¥3-5K start</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Avg fare</div><div class="car-stat-val">¥250-400</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Taxi base</div><div class="car-stat-val">¥500 / 1km</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="car-providers">
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.global.jr-central.co.jp/en/info/icca/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Suica info</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://go.goinc.jp/en/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> GO Taxi app</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://m.uber.com/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Uber Tokyo</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="car-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="car-head">
          <div class="car-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-bus"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h4>Westin Miyako Kyoto → KIX airport</h4>
            <div class="car-leg">Sat Jul 25 · Departure transfer</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="car-detail">Hotel shuttle/taxi to Kyoto Station, then JR Haruka Express → Kansai Airport (~75 min total to platform + ride). Easiest with luggage. Alternative: pre-book a private van Kyoto → KIX door-to-door. Time the departure for a 3h pre-flight window — confirm the KIX departure time once the open-jaw return is ticketed.</p>
        <div class="car-stats">
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Time</div><div class="car-stat-val">~75 min rail</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Haruka</div><div class="car-stat-val">¥3.6K × 4</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Van est.</div><div class="car-stat-val">¥30K (₹17K)</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="car-providers">
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.westjr.co.jp/global/en/ticket/pass/haruka/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Haruka Express</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.klook.com/en-IN/activity/8164-kansai-airport-private-transfer-kyoto/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Klook van</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="car-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="car-head">
          <div class="car-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-car"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h4>BLR T2 → Home (return)</h4>
            <div class="car-leg">Sat Jul 25 · 03:00 → 04:30 home</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="car-detail">The open-jaw return lands at BLR late on Jul 25 / early Jul 26 depending on the routing. By the time the family clears immigration + bags, pre-book Uber Reserve from BLR for the homebound leg — much easier than queueing at the kerbside in the dark with two sleepy kids.</p>
        <div class="car-stats">
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Distance</div><div class="car-stat-val">~40 km</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Drive</div><div class="car-stat-val">~1 hr</div></div>
          <div class="car-stat"><div class="car-stat-lbl">Est.</div><div class="car-stat-val">₹1.8-2.5K</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="car-providers">
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://m.uber.com/reserve/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Uber Reserve</a>
          <a class="provider-link" href="https://www.savaari.com/airport-transfer/bengaluru-airport-cabs/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Savaari</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== LIVE VEG RESTAURANTS (SerpAPI Google Local) ========== -->
<section class="veg-section" id="veg-restaurants">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="section-eyebrow">Live veg dining</div>
        <h2>Vegetarian-safe restaurants <em>near each stay</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>Pulled live via Google Local for the exact stops. Tokyo + Kyoto have a real (and growing) Indian-veg + shojin-ryori scene. Day trips (Fuji/Kawaguchiko, Hakone, Kamakura, Nara) lean on konbini + the veg-adaptable spots noted in each day card. Click any to open in Google Maps for hours, photos, and directions.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-map-split">
     <div class="section-map-split__list">
    <h3 style="font-family: Fraunces, serif; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px; margin-top: 16px;">Tokyo · near JW Marriott (Roppongi) + Shibuya/Ginza/Akihabara</h3>
    <div class="veg-grid" id="veg-tokyo" data-lat="35.6595" data-lon="139.7005" data-radius="3500" data-city="Tokyo" data-country="Japan">
      <div class="veg-loading">Loading veg restaurants…</div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="font-family: Fraunces, serif; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px; margin-top: 48px;">Kyoto · near Westin Miyako + Gion + Higashiyama</h3>
    <div class="veg-grid" id="veg-kyoto" data-lat="35.0117" data-lon="135.7681" data-radius="3500" data-city="Kyoto" data-country="Japan">
      <div class="veg-loading">Loading veg restaurants…</div>
    </div>

    <p class="veg-attribution">
      Live data via Google Local (SerpAPI). Names, hours, and ratings refresh on every page load — verify with the restaurant directly before going (some shojin-ryori places require advance booking by 1-2 days).
    </p>
     </div>
     <aside class="section-map-split__map" data-trip-map="restaurants" aria-label="Map of vegetarian restaurants"></aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== DOOR TO DOOR ========== -->
<section class="door" id="door-to-door">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="section-eyebrow">Door to door</div>
        <h2>Front door to <em>front door</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>Every leg of the trip with timing, links, and what to carry. Built for the locked single-base Tokyo (10n) → Kyoto (4n) shape — open-jaw, arrive NRT, depart KIX.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="door-flow">

      <!-- Stage 1: Home → BLR T2 -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-home"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">Home → BLR T2</div>
          <span class="stage-when">Fri Jul 10 · 02:30 dep · 03:30 arrival</span>
        </div>
        <div data-route="car"
          data-from="HOME" data-from-label="Bangalore" data-from-time="Fri · 02:30"
          data-to="BLR" data-to-label="BLR T2" data-to-time="Fri · 03:30"
          data-duration="1h · ~40 km"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Pre-book Uber Reserve <strong style="color: var(--saffron-soft);">48h prior</strong>. Family of 4 + 4 large suitcases needs Uber XL or Ola Prime SUV. Reach BLR T2 by 03:30 for a 06:00 international departure — at least 3h before takeoff.</p>
        <div class="stage-body">
          <div class="stage-col">
            <h6>Check before leaving</h6>
            <ul>
              <li>Passports for all 4 with eVisa printed (validity 6+ months)</li>
              <li>Hotel + flight + Klook + Shinkansen confirmations on phone + 1 printed copy</li>
              <li>Web check-in done T-1 day · seat selection confirmed</li>
              <li>Wallet · ₹15K cash · ¥30K (or forex card pre-loaded) · cards activated for international use</li>
              <li>Power: phones + power banks ≤27000mAh in carry-on, USB-C cables, Japan-compatible adapters (Type A — same as US, no adapter needed for two-pin)</li>
              <li>Travel insurance papers · pediatric script copies</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-col">
            <h6>Carry vs check</h6>
            <ul>
              <li>Carry-on: docs, electronics, ORS, kid snacks, change of clothes for 6yo</li>
              <li>Checked: bulk clothes, toiletries, gifts, summer light layers (Tokyo Jul = 30°C+)</li>
              <li>Each adult 23kg + each kid 23kg = 92kg checked allowance (Malaysia Airlines economy)</li>
              <li>Liquids ≤100ml each in transparent pouch (carry-on rule, applied at KUL too)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://m.uber.com/reserve/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Uber Reserve</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://book.olacabs.com/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Ola Prime</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.savaari.com/airport-transfer/bengaluru-airport-cabs/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Savaari</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 2: BLR T2 → boarding -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-luggage"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">BLR T2 — international check-in to gate</div>
          <span class="stage-when">03:30 → 06:00 boarding</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">International terminal at T2. Malaysia Airlines counters typically open ~3.5h before departure. Use Family-with-Kids security lane. After security, head to lounge for breakfast — flight breakfast on MH economy is ~07:30 KUL time which is after takeoff with kids already drowsy.</p>
        <div class="stage-body">
          <div class="stage-col">
            <h6>Lounges (Amex Plat covers all 4)</h6>
            <ul>
              <li>Adani Lounge — international departures, level 4 (Priority Pass + Amex Plat)</li>
              <li>080 Lounge — Plaza Premium, alternative if Adani is full</li>
              <li>Light breakfast + work corner + kid play area + nap zone</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-col">
            <h6>Practical</h6>
            <ul>
              <li>Confirm passport stamping (immigration officer) before lounge — saves a 20-min queue at boarding</li>
              <li>Power banks must be in carry-on, not checked (≤27000mAh)</li>
              <li>Strollers tag-on-aircraft for the 6yo if needed</li>
              <li>Boarding 30 min before; gates close 10 min before departure</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 3: BLR → KUL flight -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-plane"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">BLR → KUL · MH 193</div>
          <span class="stage-when">06:00 → 12:30 KUL · 4h 30m</span>
        </div>
        <div data-route="flight"
          data-from="BLR" data-from-label="Bangalore" data-from-time="Fri · 06:00"
          data-to="KUL" data-to-label="Kuala Lumpur" data-to-time="Fri · 12:30 (KUL)"
          data-duration="4h 30m · MH 193"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Malaysia Airlines, Boeing 738. Pre-order Asian Vegetarian Meal (AVML) when booking. Tablet for kids essential — IFE library is decent but limited. KUL layover ~3h is right-sized: long enough to clear transit security, short enough to keep kid morale up.</p>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.malaysiaairlines.com/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Malaysia Airlines</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.skyscanner.co.in/transport/flights/blr/nrt/260710/?adults=2&children=2" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-search"/></svg> Skyscanner</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 4: KUL transit -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-luggage"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">KUL — transit</div>
          <span class="stage-when">12:30 → 15:30 KUL · 3h layover</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Stay airside (transit). KLIA Plaza Premium Lounge (Amex Plat) for shower + lunch — kids will need a stretch. KLIA → KLIA2 transfer is automated train, ~3 min. Re-check security at gate. Verify boarding gate has changed (common at KUL).</p>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.malaysiaairports.com.my/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> KLIA map</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.plazapremiumlounge.com/en-uk/find/asia/malaysia/kuala-lumpur/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Plaza Premium KUL</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 5: KUL → NRT flight -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-plane"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">KUL → NRT · MH 70</div>
          <span class="stage-when">15:30 KUL → 23:55 NRT · 7h</span>
        </div>
        <div data-route="flight"
          data-from="KUL" data-from-label="Kuala Lumpur" data-from-time="Fri · 15:30 (KUL)"
          data-to="NRT" data-to-label="Tokyo Narita" data-to-time="Fri · 23:55 (JST)"
          data-duration="7h · MH 70"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Boeing 738 (some routes A330). AVML pre-ordered. Kids will likely sleep most of this leg — bring a thin blanket each. Land at Narita at midnight: immigration clears in ~30 min for foreign passports (Trusted Traveler does not apply for Indians yet). Bag claim ~20 min. Outside the gate by 01:00.</p>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.malaysiaairlines.com/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Malaysia Airlines</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.narita-airport.jp/en/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Narita Arrivals</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 6: NRT → Tokyo hotel -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-car"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">NRT → JW Marriott Tokyo (Roppongi)</div>
          <span class="stage-when">Sat Jul 11 · 01:00 → 02:30</span>
        </div>
        <div data-route="car"
          data-from="NRT" data-from-label="Narita" data-from-time="Sat · 01:00"
          data-to="HOTEL" data-to-label="JW Marriott Tokyo" data-to-time="Sat · 02:30"
          data-duration="1h 30m · ~75 km · pre-booked van"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Pre-book a private van via Klook or Welcome Pickups. Driver waits with name-board at arrivals (Trusted Vendor zone). <strong style="color: var(--saffron-soft);">This is the office-provided hotel</strong> — book the 2 arrival nights (Jul 11–13) on Bonvoy points and ask the hotel to link them to the office reservation (Jul 13–21) so it's one seamless 10-night stay with no room move. Titanium gets late check-out + suite upgrade subject to availability. Crash, hydrate, reset for Day 1.</p>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.klook.com/en-IN/activity/2107-narita-airport-private-transfer-tokyo/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Klook van</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.welcomepickups.com/tokyo/airport-taxi/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Welcome Pickups</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/tyojw-jw-marriott-hotel-tokyo/overview/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-bed"/></svg> JW Marriott Tokyo</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 7: Day trips from Tokyo -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-mountain"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">Day trips from Tokyo — Fuji · Hakone · Kamakura</div>
          <span class="stage-when">Jul 12 → Jul 20 · same JW Marriott base every night</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Because the office covers the JW Marriott Jul 13–21, every nature trip is a <strong style="color: var(--saffron-soft);">round-trip day out</strong> — no ryokan night, no second hotel, no packing. Leave bags at the JW; carry a day pack. <strong>Mt Fuji / Kawaguchiko</strong> (Jul 17): ~2h via Fuji Excursion limited express from Shinjuku — go on a clear-forecast morning. <strong>Kamakura</strong> (Jul 18): ~1h on the JR Yokosuka line from Tokyo Station — the easy one. <strong>Hakone loop</strong> (Jul 19): Romance Car to Hakone-Yumoto, then the Free Pass loop (Tozan rail → ropeway → Owakudani → Lake Ashi pirate ship), back to Tokyo by night — or swap for a relaxed Tokyo day if energy is low.</p>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.jreast.co.jp/multi/en/pass/fuji_excursion.html" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Fuji Excursion</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.odakyu.jp/english/romancecar/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Romance Car</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.odakyu.jp/english/passes/hakone/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Hakone Free Pass</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 8: Tokyo → Kyoto Shinkansen -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-train"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">Tokyo → Kyoto · Nozomi Shinkansen</div>
          <span class="stage-when">Tue Jul 21 · 11:00 → 13:15 Kyoto</span>
        </div>
        <div data-route="train"
          data-from="TYO" data-from-label="Tokyo Station" data-from-time="Tue · 11:00"
          data-to="KYO" data-to-label="Kyoto Station" data-to-time="Tue · 13:15"
          data-duration="2h 15m · Nozomi · 520 km"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Last JW Marriott breakfast + checkout, then the midday Nozomi. Reserved seats on Smart-EX. Pick the right (D/E) side coming from Tokyo for the Mt. Fuji view (~40 min in, weather-dependent). Buy bento at Tokyo Station's Ekiben market — kid-friendly options abound. Forward the two big bags a day ahead (Jul 20, from the JW concierge) via Yamato (¥2K/bag) to the Westin Miyako so you travel light on the train.</p>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://smart-ex.jp/en/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Smart-EX</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.kuronekoyamato.co.jp/en/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Yamato luggage</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Tokyo+Station/Kyoto+Station" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-route"/></svg> Route</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 9: Kyoto → KIX airport -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-train"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">Westin Miyako Kyoto → Kansai Airport (KIX)</div>
          <span class="stage-when">Sat Jul 25 · 06:00 → 07:30 KIX</span>
        </div>
        <div data-route="train"
          data-from="KYO" data-from-label="Kyoto Station" data-from-time="Sat · 06:00"
          data-to="KIX" data-to-label="Kansai Airport" data-to-time="Sat · 07:30"
          data-duration="1h 15m · Haruka Express"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Early start (request a Westin breakfast box the night before). Hotel taxi to Kyoto Station, then the first <strong>Haruka Limited Express</strong> to KIX (~75 min, reserved seats). The early flight is deliberate — it gets the family home to Bangalore the same day (Jul 25 evening) instead of the small hours of Jul 26. Open-jaw payoff: you fly out of Kansai with zero Shinkansen backtrack to Tokyo. Light bags — no forwarding on the way home.</p>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.westjr.co.jp/global/en/ticket/limited-express/haruka/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Haruka Express</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.kansai-airport.or.jp/en" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> KIX Airport</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 10: KIX → KUL → BLR -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-plane"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">KIX → KUL → BLR · open-jaw return</div>
          <span class="stage-when">Sat Jul 25 · 10:00 KIX → Sat Jul 25 · 23:30 BLR</span>
        </div>
        <div data-route="flight"
          data-from="KIX" data-from-label="Kansai Airport" data-from-time="Sat · 10:00 (JST)"
          data-to="BLR" data-to-label="Bangalore" data-to-time="Sat · 23:30 (IST)"
          data-duration="~14h total · via KUL"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Return leg of the open-jaw (booked as a multi-city BLR→NRT + KIX→BLR — price it against a round-trip NRT before ticketing; it's usually within a few % and saves the backtrack day). Malaysia Airlines KIX → KUL, connect KUL → BLR. AVML pre-ordered both legs. KUL layover covered by Amex Plat lounge access.</p>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.malaysiaairlines.com/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Malaysia Airlines</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.skyscanner.co.in/transport/flights/kix/blr/260725/?adults=2&children=2" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-search"/></svg> Skyscanner</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stage 11: BLR → Home -->
      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-home"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">BLR → Home</div>
          <span class="stage-when">Sun Jul 26 · 00:00 → 01:30</span>
        </div>
        <div data-route="car"
          data-from="BLR" data-from-label="BLR T2" data-from-time="Sun · 00:00"
          data-to="HOME" data-to-label="Bangalore" data-to-time="Sun · 01:30"
          data-duration="1h · ~40 km"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Pre-book Uber Reserve from BLR for the homebound leg too — much easier than queueing at the kerbside late at night with two sleepy kids. Pre-stocked groceries at home (set on T-1) save a tired-morning problem. Landing Saturday night leaves all of Sunday — and the following days — as a jet-lag reset buffer well before school resumes.</p>
        <div class="link-chips">
          <a class="chip" href="https://m.uber.com/reserve/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Uber Reserve</a>
          <a class="chip" href="https://www.savaari.com/airport-transfer/bengaluru-airport-cabs/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Savaari</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== VISA + HEALTH + INSURANCE ========== -->
<section class="visa-section" id="visa-health">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="section-eyebrow">Paperwork + safety</div>
        <h2>Visa, insurance, health · <em>before you go</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>Japan is one of the safest destinations on earth — but Indian passport holders need an eVisa, kid vaccines need a pediatrician sign-off, and travel insurance is genuinely worth the ₹3-5K. Don't skip these.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-grid">

      <div class="visa-card">
        <h5><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg> Japan eVisa (Indian passports)</h5>
        <p>Japan accepts eVisa applications from Indian citizens since 2024 — single-entry tourist eVisa is the standard. <strong>Apply 4 weeks before departure</strong> — average processing 5-10 working days. Apply for all 4 family members in one batch.</p>
        <div class="meta">
          <span>Cost: <strong>FREE</strong> for Indians (eVisa fee waived)</span>
          <span>Validity: 90 days from issue</span>
          <span>Stay: up to 30 days</span>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://www.evisa.mofa.go.jp/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Apply on MOFA eVisa portal</a>
          <a href="https://www.in.emb-japan.go.jp/itpr_en/visa.html" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Embassy India</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="visa-card">
        <h5><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg> Travel insurance · 3 options surfaced</h5>
        <p>Get comprehensive coverage covering medical (₹50L+), trip cancellation, baggage loss, and adventure activity riders (Mt. Fuji ropeway, Hakone trails). 16-day coverage for family of 4 ≈ ₹4-6K total.</p>
        <div class="meta">
          <span>Required: <strong>Yes (medical proof at immigration on request)</strong></span>
          <span>Cost: <strong>₹4-6K family / 16 days</strong></span>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://www.tataaig.com/travel-insurance/japan-travel-insurance" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Tata AIG · Japan plan</a>
          <a href="https://www.iciciprulife.com/travel-insurance.html" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> ICICI Lombard</a>
          <a href="https://www.policybazaar.com/travel-insurance/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Policybazaar (compare)</a>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top:8px; font-size:12px; color: var(--ink-soft); font-style: italic;">Compare 3+ before buying. Look for: pre-existing conditions covered (Y/N), kid coverage, USD vs INR settlement, network hospital list in Japan.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="visa-card">
        <h5><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg> Vaccinations &amp; medication</h5>
        <p><strong>Always check with your pediatrician</strong> before final dosing decisions. Routine kid vaccines (MMR, DPT, Polio, Hep A/B, Typhoid) should be up-to-date. Japan does not require any specific travel-vax for tourists from India.</p>
        <div class="meta">
          <span>Carry: <strong>paracetamol syrup, ORS, anti-diarrheal, motion-sickness</strong></span>
          <span>Heat: Kyoto Jul highs 30-33°C; Tokyo 28-30°C; humid</span>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://www.cdc.gov/travel/destinations/traveler/none/japan" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> CDC Japan</a>
          <a href="https://www.mofa.go.jp/j_info/visit/medical/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> MOFA medical info</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="visa-card">
        <h5><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> eSIM · stay connected</h5>
        <p>Japan WiFi is patchy outside hotels; eSIM beats pocket WiFi rentals for a family of 4 (1 eSIM per phone). Ubigi 10GB / 30 days is plenty for navigation + Maps + WhatsApp. Activate the eSIM before you fly so it auto-connects on landing.</p>
        <div class="meta">
          <span>Cost: <strong>₹1-2K per phone</strong></span>
          <span>Activation: at least 24h before</span>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://cellulardata.ubigi.com/japan/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Ubigi Japan</a>
          <a href="https://www.airalo.com/japan-esim" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Airalo Japan</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="visa-card">
        <h5><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg> Safety + emergency</h5>
        <p>Japan ranks #1 globally on safety for tourists. Crime rate is negligible. Real risks: heat exhaustion, getting lost in Shinjuku, queue confusion at major shrines. Police: <strong>110</strong>. Ambulance + Fire: <strong>119</strong>. English-speaking line at major hospitals.</p>
        <div class="meta">
          <span>Hospital · St. Luke's Tokyo (English)</span>
          <span>India embassy Tokyo: +81-3-3262-2391</span>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://hospital.luke.ac.jp/eng/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> St. Luke's Tokyo</a>
          <a href="https://www.indembassy-tokyo.gov.in/" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> India Embassy Tokyo</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="visa-card">
        <h5><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-thermo"/></svg> Heat &amp; air quality</h5>
        <p>Climate-model projection (May-30 refresh, EC_Earth3P_HR): Tokyo highs 28-30°C, lows 22-25, with a heavy rain spike around Jul 22 (~44 mm). Kyoto runs hotter — highs 30-33°C — and the inland basin traps heat, so the 6yo will wilt. Hakone is cooler (26-29°C) but expect rain Jul 21-22. Real heat-stroke risk in Kyoto: anchor outdoor activities pre-09:30 or post-17:00. Mid-day = museums, malls, indoor lunches. AQI typically 50-80 (good) per IQAir.</p>
        <div class="meta">
          <span>ORS sachets: 2/kid/day</span>
          <span>Cooling towels: ₹500 from Tokyu Hands</span>
          <span>Pace: 1 anchor + 1 light per day max</span>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://www.jma.go.jp/jma/indexe.html" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Japan Met Agency</a>
          <a href="https://www.iqair.com/japan/tokyo" target="_blank"><svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-arrow-up-right"/></svg> Tokyo AQI live</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== HERITAGE / VEG ANCHORS ========== -->
<section class="anchors-section" id="anchors">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="section-eyebrow">Vegetarian-safe + heritage</div>
        <h2>Local specialties <em>worth seeking out</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>Japan is more vegetarian-accommodating than most realize — but it requires planning. Below are the dish + temple anchors to plan around (book ahead where noted), plus Indian-veg fallbacks for kid days when Japanese cuisine has been "enough".</p>
    </div>

    <div class="anchor-grid">

      <div class="anchor-card-wrap kind-food">
        <div class="anchor-card">
          <div class="anchor-head">
            <div>
              <div class="name">Buddhist temple cuisine</div>
              <div class="where">Kyoto · Tenryu-ji "Shigetsu"</div>
            </div>
            <span class="anchor-kind">Restaurant</span>
          </div>
          <hr class="anchor-divider">
          <div class="anchor-section-label">What to expect</div>
          <ul class="anchor-checklist">
            <li>Multi-course Zen meal, entirely plant-based</li>
            <li>No garlic / onion — Shojin tradition</li>
            <li>Books up 1-2 weeks ahead</li>
            <li>Kid-acceptable: ask for less wasabi</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="anchor-meta">
            <div class="anchor-meta-headline">Shojin Ryori</div>
            <span class="anchor-meta-sub">most "real" cultural meal of the trip</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a class="anchor-cta" href="https://www.tenryuji.com/en/shigetsu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book Shigetsu</a>
        <div class="anchor-secondary-links">
          <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/Shigetsu+Tenryu-ji+Arashiyama" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Maps ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="anchor-card-wrap kind-food">
        <div class="anchor-card">
          <div class="anchor-head">
            <div>
              <div class="name">Tofu skin · Kyoto staple</div>
              <div class="where">Kyoto · Gion · Higashiyama</div>
            </div>
            <span class="anchor-kind">Restaurant</span>
          </div>
          <hr class="anchor-divider">
          <div class="anchor-section-label">What to expect</div>
          <ul class="anchor-checklist">
            <li>Soy milk skin — silky, mild, kid-friendly</li>
            <li>Yuba Kichi (Higashiyama) — casual sets</li>
            <li>Tousuiro (Pontocho) — kaiseki-style</li>
            <li>Request "no dashi" sets in advance</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="anchor-meta">
            <div class="anchor-meta-headline">Yuba</div>
            <span class="anchor-meta-sub">silky tofu skin · Kyoto specialty</span>
