<section class="post-trip" id="post-trip">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="section-eyebrow">After the trip</div>
        <h2>Log it, <em>so we plan better</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>When you return: paste the prompt below into Claude Code in this project. The system appends this trip to your visited journal, captures actual costs, saves lessons learned, and updates recommendation scoring for next time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="post-grid">
      <div>
        <pre class="post-prompt" id="post-trip-prompt">Log my completed trip: 2026-07-tokyo-koyoto-and-other-famous (Tokyo single base + Kyoto, Jul 10–25 2026, family of 4).

I'll provide:
- Actual flight costs (₹) — open-jaw BLR→NRT + KIX→BLR, outbound + return separately
- Actual hotel costs (₹) — JW Marriott Tokyo (2 arrival nights on points; Jul 13–21 office-provided/free) + Westin Miyako Kyoto (paid + points + cert applied yes/no, which night)
- Bonvoy nights stayed + points earned
- Marriott 40K cert: used or unused (and where)
- DisneySea (Jul 16 workshop-day family outing): worth it / kid verdict
- Actual activities + food + transfers + Shinkansen + day-trip rail (Fuji/Hakone/Kamakura/Nara) spend
- Top 3 highlights · top 1 regret
- The 6yo's "wall" moment (when energy gave out) — informs future kid-pace planning
- Photos (URLs or local paths)
- Anything that will help future planning (e.g., "Owakudani sulphur eggs were a hit; Ghibli Museum was sold out — book the lottery earlier next time")

Then:
1. Append a row to trips/_shared/data/visited.json with: city Tokyo + Kyoto, country Japan, month Jul, year 2026.
2. Update .workspace/loyalty.md with new balances + cert status (mark as used/expired).
3. Append lessons-learned to .workspace/user_travel_prefs.md under a "Trip lessons" section if non-trivial — heat tolerance, kid-pace, restaurant winners, transit notes.
4. Update trips/2026-07-tokyo-koyoto-and-other-famous/index.html: add a "Completed" status badge + actuals-vs-estimates row in costs section + a "Highlights" gallery.
5. Update trips/index.html: change card status from Active to Archived; bump trips-logged counter.
6. Trigger a regeneration of trips/_shared/data/recommendations.json so the next-trip suggestions reflect the new visit (12-month exclusion for Japan).

Read .workspace/user_travel_prefs.md for hard rules.</pre>
        <div style="margin-top: 16px; display: flex; gap: 12px;">
          <button class="btn btn-saffron btn-sm" onclick="copyPostPrompt()">
            <svg class="icon icon-sm"><use href="#i-sparkles"/></svg>
            Copy post-trip prompt
          </button>
          <span id="post-copy-state" style="font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-soft); align-self: center;"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="post-fields">
        <div class="post-field">
          <div class="post-field-lbl">What you'll capture</div>
          <div class="post-field-val">Actual costs vs estimates</div>
          <div class="post-field-help">Flights, hotels, activities, transfers, food. Each line item updates the budget envelope's lessons tab.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="post-field">
          <div class="post-field-lbl">What you'll capture</div>
          <div class="post-field-val">Loyalty deltas</div>
          <div class="post-field-help">Bonvoy nights + points earned · 40K cert used Y/N · Avios redeemed if any.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="post-field">
          <div class="post-field-lbl">What you'll capture</div>
          <div class="post-field-val">Highlights + regrets</div>
          <div class="post-field-help">Best meal · best moment · what to skip. The 6yo's "wall" timing is gold for future itineraries.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="post-field">
          <div class="post-field-lbl">What you'll capture</div>
          <div class="post-field-val">Photos + memories</div>
          <div class="post-field-help">Drop URLs or local paths · the system embeds them into a gallery on this trip page.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== WHY ========== -->
<section class="why">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="section-eyebrow">Designed around</div>
        <h2>Three things that <em>matter</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>Defaults set to your family pace, not a generic Tokyo-influencer itinerary. Heat, kid-energy, and loyalty leverage shape every recommendation.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="why-grid">
      <div class="why-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="why-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-thermo"/></svg></div>
        <h5>Heat-aware pace</h5>
        <p>Tokyo Jul = 32-35°C + humid. Anchor outdoor activities pre-09:30 or post-17:00. Mid-day = museums, malls, AC. The 6yo gets a daily nap window — non-negotiable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="why-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="why-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-sparkles"/></svg></div>
        <h5>Kid-anchor variety</h5>
        <p>Shrine + bullet train + ramen + monkeys + ropeway + Pokemon + DisneySea. Cultural depth without the kid revolt — every "adult day" is bracketed by a kid-magnet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="why-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="why-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-key"/></svg></div>
        <h5>Loyalty leverage</h5>
        <p>The office covers 8 Tokyo nights at the JW Marriott, which frees the Bonvoy 40K cert + Titanium balance to cover all 4 Kyoto nights at the Westin Miyako. Net: only 2 self-paid points-nights all trip — turns balances into real value.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

